  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Norway-CAFOD Strategic Partnership 2023-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Norway and CAFOD have identified that it is mutually beneficial to enter into a strategic partnership, the basis of which is outlined in the Memorandum of Understanding, from August 2023- August 2026. Mutual benefits will be realised as the two agencies work together across a number of organisational functions with a view to enhancing and developing each organisation&#x2019;s ability to deliver its humanitarian function. While the primary function of the MoU remains around joint humanitarian working, we will work to ensure we share cross organisation information and on our advocacy and development programmes and, where appropriate, develop joint working. A range of specific activities will be agreed mutually and be delivered in partnership, with a particular focus on:

- Institutional humanitarian fund-raising and joint humanitarian programming, 
- Humanitarian advocacy, 
- Humanitarian Capacity Building,
- Joint surge capacity development,
- Joint funding of two position- CVA Advisor and Funding Officer
- Joint country focus. 

The anticipated outcomes arising from this partnership will include greater humanitarian and, where appropriate development programme impact, organisational strengthening, enhanced organisational effectiveness and operational efficiencies.   MOU is to be renegotiated every year at least three months before the end of the current year.  CAFOD will provide &#xa3;45,000 each year to support the joint funding of a Funding Officer, based in Oslo- no date for this payment is given in the MOU.</narrative>
  </description>
